sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: DNS cache expiry does not end existing connections
  accDescr: Client queries a recursive resolver, which queries the authority on a miss or expiry; an authority update leaves the eligible cached answer and an existing socket with independent lifetimes.
participant C as Client
  participant R as Resolver
  participant A as Authority
  C->>R: t=0: A query
  R->>A: Cache miss
  A-->>R: old, TTL 60
  R-->>C: old
  Note over C,A: t=5: client opens connection to old
  Note over C,A: t=10: authority changes to new
  C->>R: t=30: A query
  R-->>C: Cached old
  C->>R: t=61: A query
  R->>A: Expired, refresh
  A-->>R: new
  R-->>C: new
  Note over C,A: Existing old connection has its own lifetime
